**Public visibility is not a license.** This template and any page made from it do not replace a signed agreement, controlling policy, applicable law, or qualified review.

## Plain-language summary

In two or three sentences, explain:

- what issue this page covers;
- who can use the process;
- what this process may and may not decide;
- the safest next action.

<Columns cols={2}>
  <Card title="Covered" icon="circle-check">
    Replace with the exact rights, licensing, policy, complaint, or support scope supported by the governing source.
  </Card>
  <Card title="Not established" icon="ban">
    Do not imply ownership, permission, clearance, entitlement, legal sufficiency, refund, remedy, response time, or outcome without exact authority and evidence.
  </Card>
</Columns>

## Scope and applicability

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Rights or licensing">
    Identify the asset, territory, term, media, use, parties, governing instrument, and excluded uses. If any element is unknown, mark it `unresolved`.
  </Tab>
  <Tab title="Policy or complaint">
    Identify the applicable policy version, conduct or decision in scope, submitting party, and review boundary.
  </Tab>
  <Tab title="Support">
    Identify the affected product or service, account or order reference boundary, observed symptom, and support channel. Do not publish personal, payment, credential, or restricted evidence.
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

State jurisdiction, territory, effective period, eligibility, exclusions, and qualified-review triggers only when supported by the controlling source.

